WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:04.017
Imagine a housing proposal on a Torrance corridor.

2
00:00:04.017 --> 00:00:05.588
The elevations are unfamiliar.

3
00:00:05.588 --> 00:00:09.671
A commissioner wants the facade to feel more compatible with nearby buildings.

4
00:00:09.671 --> 00:00:19.878
Staff points to a state streamlined pathway and asks a different question: does the proposal comply with the objective standards that were in effect when the application became subject to review?

5
00:00:19.878 --> 00:00:24.066
In that setting, taste is not a standard, and delay can change the legal result.

6
00:00:24.066 --> 00:00:27.521
The commission needs a method that works before the clock expires.

7
00:00:27.521 --> 00:00:32.215
This episode is preparation, not legal advice about any application or deadline.

8
00:00:32.215 --> 00:00:38.435
California processing laws contain definitions, exceptions, tolling rules, and pathway-specific timelines.

9
00:00:38.435 --> 00:00:39.491
They change often.

10
00:00:39.491 --> 00:00:47.002
The current statute, HCD guidance, local ordinance, complete project record, and advice from the Torrance city attorney control.

11
00:00:47.002 --> 00:00:52.107
An objective standard involves no personal or subjective judgment by a public official.

12
00:00:52.107 --> 00:01:00.205
A developer, staff member, commissioner, and court should be able to apply the same text to the same facts and reach a predictable result.

13
00:01:00.205 --> 00:01:07.892
Dimensions, ratios, listed materials, mapped areas, measurable performance levels, and clearly defined procedures can be objective.

14
00:01:07.892 --> 00:01:15.402
Words such as harmonious, high quality, appropriate, or compatible usually need measurable content before they can do that work.

15
00:01:15.402 --> 00:01:17.867
Objectivity is not the same as simplicity.

16
00:01:17.867 --> 00:01:22.679
A standard can use a formula, reference a map, or require a technical measurement.

17
00:01:22.679 --> 00:01:25.613
But the inputs and decision rule must be knowable.

18
00:01:25.613 --> 00:01:28.664
A standard that says preserve privacy is subjective.

19
00:01:28.664 --> 00:01:38.111
A standard that limits specified upper-story window placement within a measured distance of a residential property line is more likely to be applied objectively.

20
00:01:38.111 --> 00:01:40.517
Objective standards still express policy.

21
00:01:40.517 --> 00:01:49.436
A city can decide where entrances belong, how blank walls are limited, what setbacks apply, how trees are replaced, or how ground floors meet sidewalks.

22
00:01:49.436 --> 00:01:53.074
The legislative stage is where officials debate those choices.

23
00:01:53.074 --> 00:01:59.998
Once a qualifying ministerial application arrives, the job is consistent application, not project-by-project redesign.

24
00:01:59.998 --> 00:02:02.129
Build every standard from four parts.

25
00:02:02.129 --> 00:02:03.339
First is the trigger.

26
00:02:03.339 --> 00:02:07.947
State exactly which projects, lots, frontages, or building elements are covered.

27
00:02:07.947 --> 00:02:09.041
Second is the rule.

28
00:02:09.041 --> 00:02:11.345
Use a number, defined category, or test.

29
00:02:11.345 --> 00:02:13.189
Third is the measurement method.

30
00:02:13.189 --> 00:02:17.681
State where measurement begins and ends and which document supplies the input.

31
00:02:17.681 --> 00:02:19.179
Fourth is the consequence.

32
00:02:19.179 --> 00:02:22.520
Explain what revision or condition resolves noncompliance.

33
00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:24.882
Test a draft standard against edge cases.

34
00:02:24.882 --> 00:02:26.552
What happens on a corner lot?

35
00:02:26.552 --> 00:02:27.934
Which street is primary?

36
00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:29.317
How are slopes measured?

37
00:02:29.317 --> 00:02:30.814
What if two maps disagree?

38
00:02:30.814 --> 00:02:34.847
Does a percentage apply to the entire facade or only the ground floor?

39
00:02:34.847 --> 00:02:39.339
If staff has to invent an answer during review, the standard was not finished.

40
00:02:39.339 --> 00:02:40.722
Avoid hidden discretion.

41
00:02:40.722 --> 00:02:45.963
A list of acceptable materials followed by or similar gives the reviewer a subjective gate.

42
00:02:45.963 --> 00:02:50.687
A requirement for substantial variation is unclear unless variation is quantified.

43
00:02:50.687 --> 00:02:58.117
A design-review body cannot transform an objective pathway into a discretionary one by asking whether the building is attractive.

44
00:02:58.117 --> 00:03:01.804
The processing clock makes this drafting discipline operational.

45
00:03:01.804 --> 00:03:05.202
Different laws use different starting points and deadlines.

46
00:03:05.202 --> 00:03:08.313
The Permit Streamlining Act governs many applications.

47
00:03:08.313 --> 00:03:14.130
The Housing Accountability Act creates timing and consistency rules for housing development projects.

48
00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:21.215
The streamlined ministerial approval process associated with Senate Bill 35 and Senate Bill 423 has its own review periods.

49
00:03:21.215 --> 00:03:23.980
Other ministerial pathways have separate clocks.

50
00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:26.111
Never begin with a remembered number.

51
00:03:26.111 --> 00:03:29.567
Begin with the pathway and the event that starts the period.

52
00:03:29.567 --> 00:03:38.092
Is it receipt of an application, determination that an application is complete, submission of a preliminary application, or another statutory event?

53
00:03:38.092 --> 00:03:45.638
Then identify what the agency must complete: completeness review, written inconsistency findings, design review, or final approval.

54
00:03:45.638 --> 00:04:01.530
HCD's current streamlined ministerial materials explain that, for qualifying projects of 150 units or fewer, a jurisdiction generally has 60 days after receiving the application to determine consistency with objective standards and 90 days to complete design review.

55
00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:07.922
Larger projects generally receive 90 days for the consistency determination and 180 days for design review.

56
00:04:07.922 --> 00:04:12.104
Review of specified resubmittals is generally required within 30 days.

57
00:04:12.104 --> 00:04:16.944
Those numbers belong to that pathway and remain subject to current law and facts.

58
00:04:16.944 --> 00:04:19.871
Do not paste them onto every housing application.

59
00:04:19.871 --> 00:04:24.650
The consequence of missing a statutory consistency-review period can be serious.

60
00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:34.867
Under the streamlined process, a project may be deemed consistent with objective standards if the jurisdiction does not provide the required written documentation on time.

61
00:04:34.867 --> 00:04:39.407
A late list of concerns is not equivalent to a timely, specific explanation.

62
00:04:39.407 --> 00:04:48.608
Good written feedback identifies the exact adopted standard, states the project fact being compared, explains the measurement, and describes the conflict.

63
00:04:48.608 --> 00:04:51.475
It avoids general requests to improve character.

64
00:04:51.475 --> 00:04:56.972
If a minor correction can bring the project into compliance, say precisely what must change.

65
00:04:56.972 --> 00:05:02.110
Preserve one coordinated agency response rather than a trail of inconsistent comments.

66
00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:05.097
Objective does not mean inflexible administration.

67
00:05:05.097 --> 00:05:09.159
Staff may verify facts, perform calculations, and apply definitions.

68
00:05:09.159 --> 00:05:13.819
The city may impose compliant conditions that implement an objective standard.

69
00:05:13.819 --> 00:05:17.225
The boundary is judgment untethered to a measurable rule.

70
00:05:17.225 --> 00:05:20.690
For practical application, run a clock-and-standard drill.

71
00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:24.812
Choose a fictional 120-unit mixed-use project on Hawthorne Boulevard.

72
00:05:24.812 --> 00:05:30.308
Assume only for the exercise that counsel confirms a particular streamlined pathway applies.

73
00:05:30.308 --> 00:05:41.361
Create a clock sheet with the submission date, statutory trigger, consistency deadline, design-review deadline, resubmittal deadline, responsible reviewer, and required written product.

74
00:05:41.361 --> 00:05:45.304
Then choose five local standards and complete a compliance matrix.

75
00:05:45.304 --> 00:05:46.977
The matrix has five columns.

76
00:05:46.977 --> 00:05:48.052
Cite the standard.

77
00:05:48.052 --> 00:05:50.502
Copy only the minimum operative language.

78
00:05:50.502 --> 00:05:51.936
Record the project fact.

79
00:05:51.936 --> 00:05:53.907
Show the measurement or evidence.

80
00:05:53.907 --> 00:05:56.954
Mark comply, conflict, or insufficient information.

81
00:05:56.954 --> 00:06:03.466
For every conflict, draft one sentence that identifies the specific mismatch without adding a new preference.

82
00:06:03.466 --> 00:06:09.631
Commissioners can improve the system even when a particular application is ministerial and never reaches them.

83
00:06:09.631 --> 00:06:13.946
During ordinance work, ask whether each standard survives the edge-case test.

84
00:06:13.946 --> 00:06:16.749
Ask staff to conduct mock reviews before adoption.

85
00:06:16.749 --> 00:06:21.344
Request diagrams that illustrate measurement without replacing the governing text.

86
00:06:21.344 --> 00:06:27.285
Ask whether standards conflict across zoning, specific plans, fire requirements, and public-works manuals.

87
00:06:27.285 --> 00:06:30.312
Do not solve uncertainty by adding layers of approval.

88
00:06:30.312 --> 00:06:33.674
A required consultation can itself become a source of delay.

89
00:06:33.674 --> 00:06:37.542
Define who makes the determination and what document closes the step.

90
00:06:37.542 --> 00:06:41.465
Keep a versioned library of the standards in effect on relevant dates.

91
00:06:41.465 --> 00:06:46.957
Also separate objective planning standards from building, fire, and other health and safety rules.

92
00:06:46.957 --> 00:06:52.898
A project may be ministerial under planning law while still requiring code-compliant construction permits.

93
00:06:52.898 --> 00:06:57.886
The existence of later technical review does not authorize discretionary land-use denial.

94
00:06:57.886 --> 00:06:59.623
The city should audit outcomes.

95
00:06:59.623 --> 00:07:03.771
If every applicant misunderstands the same rule, clarify it legislatively.

96
00:07:03.771 --> 00:07:09.151
If a standard unexpectedly blocks the housing form the element assumed, evaluate the constraint.

97
00:07:09.151 --> 00:07:13.298
If staff repeatedly grants ad hoc interpretations, replace them with text.

98
00:07:13.298 --> 00:07:20.136
Predictability benefits residents as well as applicants because the public can understand what the adopted policy permits.

99
00:07:20.136 --> 00:07:24.339
Details change, especially effective dates and pathway-specific procedures.

100
00:07:24.339 --> 00:07:28.935
A timeline in a training script is a prompt to verify, not authority for a motion.

101
00:07:28.935 --> 00:07:30.501
Now three recall questions.

102
00:07:30.501 --> 00:07:31.256
Question one.

103
00:07:31.256 --> 00:07:33.808
What makes a development standard objective?

104
00:07:33.808 --> 00:07:34.214
Answer.

105
00:07:34.214 --> 00:07:42.858
It can be applied without personal or subjective judgment, using defined facts, measurements, categories, or tests that produce a predictable result.

106
00:07:42.858 --> 00:07:43.612
Question two.

107
00:07:43.612 --> 00:07:46.513
What should a timely inconsistency notice contain?

108
00:07:46.513 --> 00:07:46.919
Answer.

109
00:07:46.919 --> 00:07:53.649
The exact standard, the relevant project fact, the method of comparison, and a specific explanation of the conflict.

110
00:07:53.649 --> 00:07:54.519
Question three.

111
00:07:54.519 --> 00:07:58.232
Why must you identify the pathway before calculating a deadline?

112
00:07:58.232 --> 00:07:58.638
Answer.

113
00:07:58.638 --> 00:08:04.033
Different statutes use different triggers, tasks, time periods, exceptions, and consequences.

114
00:08:04.033 --> 00:08:07.630
A number remembered from one pathway may be wrong for another.

115
00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:13.315
Your learner artifact is the clock sheet and five-row compliance matrix for the fictional project.

116
00:08:13.315 --> 00:08:17.086
Include a box labeled assumptions requiring counsel confirmation.

117
00:08:17.086 --> 00:08:18.942
Put every date in calendar form.

118
00:08:18.942 --> 00:08:26.368
End with one proposed clarification to an objective standard that would reduce future disagreement without weakening the policy.

119
00:08:26.368 --> 00:08:46.190
This lesson draws from current California Department of Housing and Community Development materials on objective design and development standards, the Housing Accountability Act, and the Streamlined Ministerial Approval Process under Senate Bill 35 and Senate Bill 423, including HCD's 2026 fact sheets and guidance.

120
00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:52.086
It also uses the current Permit Streamlining Act framework and public local-planning practice.

121
00:08:52.086 --> 00:08:58.924
The narration is original and does not reproduce source prose, slides, maps, recordings, or proprietary data.

122
00:08:58.924 --> 00:09:07.392
Confirm every clock and standard against current statute, current HCD guidance, the applicable Torrance code, and city-attorney advice.
